Description: join OTF server thread before freeing its socket at shutdown
 ChucK::shutdown() called pthread_cancel() on the OTF listener thread and
 then immediately closed/freed carrier->otf_socket and set it to NULL,
 without waiting for the thread to terminate.  When a script finishes
 quickly the thread may not yet have reached accept() (a cancellation
 point), so it then calls ck_accept() on a freed or NULL socket and
 segfaults.  The script output is correct but chuck exits with SIGSEGV,
 causing random test suite failures (worst on ppc64el, where it made the
 build fail).  Join the thread after cancelling it.
Author: Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>
Forwarded: https://github.com/ccrma/chuck/pull/555
Last-Update: 2026-10-15

--- a/src/core/chuck.cpp
+++ b/src/core/chuck.cpp
@@ -1047,6 +1047,11 @@
         {
 #if !defined(__PLATFORM_WINDOWS__) || defined(__WINDOWS_PTHREAD__)
             pthread_cancel( m_carrier->otf_thread );
+            // wait for the thread to actually exit before freeing the socket
+            // it may be about to use; otherwise a short-lived VM can shut down
+            // before the otf thread reaches accept() and it then dereferences
+            // a freed or NULL socket, crashing on exit
+            pthread_join( m_carrier->otf_thread, NULL );
 #else
             CloseHandle( m_carrier->otf_thread ); // doesn't cancel thread
 #endif
